    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d171">

                <pb facs="0349" n="249" sameAs="frus:frus1884/pg249"/>

                <head>No. 171.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. West to Mr.
                    Frelinghuysen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1884-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 25, 1884.</date>
                        (Received June 28.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to your note of the 16th of
                    February last, I have the honor to inclose to you herewith copy of an approved
                    report of a committee of the privy council of Canada, embodying a report by the
                    minister of public works relating to the application of the Government of Canada
                    to land a cable in Washington Territory, which has been forwarded to me by the
                    Marquis of Lansdowne in reply to your above-mentioned note.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>L. S. SACKVILLE–WEST.</signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d171-a1.xml" xpointer="d171-a1"/>
            </div>
